      "id": "document:packages/opencode/specs/effect/routes.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "routes.md",
      "filePath": "packages/opencode/specs/effect/routes.md",
      "summary": "Reference for converting server route handlers to a single AppRuntime.runPromise(Effect.gen(...)) body that yields services from context instead of calling async facades one-by-one. The Hono-era instance route files it tracks (src/server/routes/instance/*.ts) have since been superseded by the Effect HttpApi handlers layout under src/server/routes/instance/httpapi/.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "effect", "http-api", "routes", "migration-plan"],
      "complexity": "simple"
    },
    {
      "id": "document:packages/opencode/specs/effect/schema.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "schema.md",
      "filePath": "packages/opencode/specs/effect/schema.md",
      "summary": "Reference for migrating domain types in packages/opencode from Zod-first definitions to Effect Schema with .zod compatibility shims derived through @opencode-ai/core/effect-zod. Includes preferred shapes (Schema.Class, TaggedErrorClass, branded IDs, named refinements), escape hatches (ZodOverride, DeepMutable), migration ordering rules, and a per-domain progress tracker covering config, leaf schema modules, session, provider, tools, and HTTP route boundaries.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "effect", "schema", "zod", "migration-plan"],
      "complexity": "complex",
      "languageNotes": "Documents the effect-zod walker that derives z.ZodType from Effect Schema while preserving JSON Schema output (type: integer, exclusiveMinimum, pattern, format: uuid), plus the ZodOverride annotation for schemas that cannot be expressed purely in Effect Schema yet."
    },
    {
      "id": "document:packages/opencode/specs/effect/server-package.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "server-package.md",
      "filePath": "packages/opencode/specs/effect/server-package.md",
      "summary": "Execution-oriented plan for extracting a future packages/server from the packages/opencode monolith as the home for HttpApi contracts, handler implementations, and OpenAPI generation. Specifies the opentunnel-style definition/api split, the phase-1 dependency rule that keeps packages/server free of packages/opencode imports, merged OpenAPI transition rules, and a nine-step incremental PR sequence starting from the experimental question slice.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "architecture", "http-api", "package-structure", "migration-plan"],
      "complexity": "complex",
      "languageNotes": "Key architectural rule: pure HttpApi/HttpApiGroup/HttpApiEndpoint contracts live separately from HttpApiBuilder.group implementations so OpenAPI can be generated from contract alone and the package stays cycle-free while packages/opencode remains the temporary host."
    },
    {
      "id": "document:packages/opencode/specs/effect/tools.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "tools.md",
      "filePath": "packages/opencode/specs/effect/tools.md",
      "summary": "Status reference for tool migration in packages/opencode: Tool.define init/execute paths already return Effect, so the remaining work is removing Promise and raw platform bridges inside tool bodies and swapping internals to AppFileSystem, HttpClient, and ChildProcessSpawner. Tracks the exported tool checklist and spot cleanups in read.ts, ripgrep, and patch application.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "effect", "tools", "migration-plan", "checklist"],
      "complexity": "moderate"
    }
  ],
